/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  MEASURED densities of the nitrogen + hydrogen binary --- SIXTEEN CITED POINTS.

  PRIMARY SOURCE, and the only thing to cite:

      R. Hernandez-Gomez, D. Tuma, A. Gomez-Hernandez, C. R. Chamorro,
      "Accurate Experimental (p, rho, T) Data for the Introduction of Hydrogen
      into the Natural Gas Grid: Thermodynamic Characterization of the
      Nitrogen-Hydrogen Binary System from 240 to 350 K and Pressures up to
      20 MPa", J. Chem. Eng. Data (2017).
      doi:10.1021/acs.jced.7b00694

  WHAT IS HERE AND WHAT IS NOT.  The published study reports 399 points.  This
  file carries SIXTEEN of them, chosen to span the pressure ladder at 250 K on
  each of the three measured compositions plus the two temperature extremes.
  Sixteen values quoted with their source is a CITATION; the 399-point table is
  the authors' arrangement and is not reproduced here.  If you want the whole
  set, obtain the ThermoML archive yourself and run

      bin/choupo-thermoml extract nitrogen --allow-mixture --into data/local/evidence

  WHY THESE AND NOT OTHERS.  The green ammonia synthesis loop in
  tutorials/plant/greenAmmoniaIndustrialN2 runs its separator near 250 K and
  its loop near 200 bar, which is exactly the corner of this study.

  THE COMPOSITION CAVEAT, WHICH THIS CASE STATES RATHER THAN HIDES.  The
  measured mixtures are NITROGEN-RICH: x(N2) = 0.50, 0.90, 0.95.  A
  stoichiometric synthesis gas is x(N2) ~ 0.25.  There is NOT ONE measured
  point between x(N2) = 0.19 and 0.31 in this dataset, so what this case tests
  is SRK's volumetric behaviour on this binary at loop T and P -- never its
  behaviour at loop COMPOSITION.  Read the verdict accordingly.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

recordType   experimentalEvidence;
property     density;
system       ( N2 H2 );
doi          "10.1021/acs.jced.7b00694";

columns
(
    { name T;     unit K;      }
    { name P;     unit kPa;    }
    { name x_N2;  unit -;      }
    { name rho;   unit kg/m3;  }
);

data
(
      240.083    19066.0    0.50008     131.423
      250.035     4998.0    0.50008      35.626
      250.038     9999.0    0.50008      69.753
      250.041    15005.0    0.50008     101.724
      250.044    19934.0    0.50008     130.700
      349.939    19885.0    0.50008      92.681
      250.043     4998.0    0.90001      62.325
      250.043     9995.0    0.90001     124.895
      250.045    15008.0    0.90001     184.307
      250.045    19653.0    0.90001     234.021
      240.046    19977.0    0.95000     266.493
      250.018     4999.0    0.95000      65.908
      250.018     9998.0    0.95000     132.641
      250.020    15009.0    0.95000     196.059
      250.023    19863.0    0.95000     251.120
      349.935    19940.0    0.95000     168.761
);
